+# Contract: verified-platforms statements in documentation
+
+**Feature**: [spec.md](../spec.md) · **Date**: 2026-10-26 · **Stage**: Phase 1 (`speckit.plan`)
+
+External interface in play: the getting-started page that a reader consults **before**
+installing, and the release downloads listing it must agree with. Normative source: spec
+FR-004, FR-005, FR-006, FR-007 and success criteria SC-003, SC-004.
+
+## D1 — The guide names platforms verifiably
+
+`docs/install/GETTING_STARTED.md` must let a reader, before installing, identify which
+platforms are **verified** (SC-003). For this feature, after implementation:
+
+- Windows 11 ARM64 is present among the platform/verification statements, with the exact
+  build-from-source steps a developer on that platform follows (FR-004) — or, in the
+  missing-observer branch, present as *not yet verified* with an honest status line and a
+  pointer to the record (FR-007).
+- The steps reference only prerequisites that are actually documented (including the MSVC
+  C++ toolset for ARM64, research R2), so the path can be followed in a single guided pass
+  with zero undocumented detours (SC-001).
+
+## D2 — Consistency with the release downloads listing (FR-005, SC-004)
+
+Zero contradictions between:
+
+- `docs/install/GETTING_STARTED.md`'s platform/verification statements, and
+- `docs/releases/0.1.0.md`'s Downloads table (`windows-x86_64`, `linux-x86_64`,
+  `SHA256SUMS.txt`).
+
+Hard rules:
+
+1. The guide may claim a **prebuilt download** for an OS + arch only if the release
+   listing contains that archive. No ARM64 archive exists, so no ARM64 download claim may
+   appear anywhere (the release notes' existing "For macOS, ARM, and other hosts, build
+   from source" line already satisfies this; keep it true).
+2. "Verified" for ARM64 is tied to the *build-from-source* method, never to an archive.
+3. If the two documents are found to disagree during implementation, the fix keeps both
+   consistent in the same change (one review, one merge); a contradiction that survives
+   the merge is a defect, not a known issue.
+
+## D3 — Every "verified" claim has an auditable transcript (FR-006)
+
+- The claim links to a dated record under `docs/acceptance/` (the ARM64 one will be
+  `windows-arm64-<YYYY-MM-DD>.md`), in the same citation style as the page's existing
+  clean-host records.
+- The record follows the format fixed in [data-model.md](../data-model.md): header table
+  (commit under test, host, toolchain, started/ended, result, secrets, cost), redundant
+  host-identity signals, binary PE-machine read, verbatim `graphhelm --version` output,
+  secrets as digests only.
+- A `verified` status is allowed only with a record whose Result is `pass`; when no
+  genuine ARM64 device was available, the record exists **instead**, names the missing
+  observer, and the platform stays unverified in the wording (FR-007, US3 scenario 2).
+- Records are append-only: supersession links to a newer transcript; older transcripts
+  are never rewritten.
+
+## D4 — Language
+
+English only, per the repository documentation rule — including the new transcript and
+any guide wording this feature adds.
