+# Contract: `graphhelm --version` on a verified host
+
+**Feature**: [spec.md](../spec.md) · **Date**: 2026-10-26 · **Stage**: Phase 1 (`speckit.plan`)
+
+This is the observable contract the ARM64 verification exercises. It describes what a
+reader can *see* when the feature works; it is not an implementation prescription.
+Normative source: spec FR-002, FR-003 and User Story 1 acceptance scenarios 1–3.
+
+## Invocation
+
+```powershell
+graphhelm --version
+```
+
+Bare invocation of the executable resolved through `PATH`; no subcommand, no flags.
+
+## Observable behavior (all must hold)
+
+| # | Aspect | Contract |
+|---|---|---|
+| C1 | Exit code | `0` |
+| C2 | stdout | Exactly **one** line matching `graphhelm <version>`, where `<version>` is semver-shaped (e.g. `0.1.0`, `0.1.1`). The exact number is observed and recorded, never asserted (research R5: the workspace version, the `VERSION` file, and an installed preview already disagree) |
+| C3 | stderr | Empty |
+| C4 | Interactivity | No prompt, no progress output; the command returns immediately |
+| C5 | Environment | Works offline on the verified host after installation; no service, account, or network dependency |
+
+## Architecture contract (the part that makes it the *ARM64* verification)
+
+| # | Signal | Source | Expectation on a genuine Windows 11 ARM64 host |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| A1 | Host process env | `$env:PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE` | `ARM64` |
+| A2 | Host system type | `Win32_ComputerSystem.SystemType` | `ARM64-based PC` |
+| A3 | Toolchain host triple | `rustup show` | default host `aarch64-pc-windows-msvc` |
+| A4 | CPU model string | `Win32_Processor.Name` | an ARM/Snapdragon part (supporting signal only — a lone WMI architecture code has been observed to mislead; research R3) |
+| A5 | Binary image type | PE COFF machine field of the resolved `graphhelm.exe` | `0xAA64` (ARM64). Anything else — in particular `0x8664` — fails FR-003 even if C1–C5 pass |
+
+**Emulation rule** (spec edge case): A1–A4 establish the *host* is genuinely ARM64 and A5
+establishes the *binary* is native. Both halves are required; an x86-64 image running
+under emulation satisfies none of the ARM64 acceptance even when it prints the right
+version line.
+
+## Negative control (User Story 1, scenario 3)
+
+The same command run on an x86-64 Windows host — expected to satisfy C1–C5 with A5 =
+`0x8664` — is explicitly **not** an ARM64 verification. Quickstart Scenario 2 runs it and
+records it as such, so a later reader cannot confuse the two outcomes.
+
+## Out of scope for this contract
+
+Anything beyond `--version`: graph commands, `serve`, Studio, MCP. Per the spec's Out of
+Scope section, the ARM64 confirmation covers only install + version behavior.
