+# Tasks: Windows 11 ARM64 CLI Install Verification
+
+**Input**: Design documents from `/specs/001-bench/`
+
+**Prerequisites**: plan.md ✓ (tech stack, structure), spec.md ✓ (3 user stories P1–P3), research.md ✓ (R1–R8), data-model.md ✓ (2 entities + state transitions), contracts/ ✓ (`version-command.md`, `verified-platform-docs.md`), quickstart.md ✓ (scenarios 1–3 + missing-observer path)
+
+**Setup note**: `.specify/scripts/` does not exist in this checkout; the stage setup JSON (`FEATURE_DIR = specs/001-bench`, `TASKS_TEMPLATE = .specify/templates/tasks-template.md`, `AVAILABLE_DOCS = []`) is treated as the `setup-tasks` output, and the design documents were listed and read directly under `specs/001-bench/`. There is no `.specify/extensions.yml`, so all extension hooks (before/after tasks) were skipped.
+
+**Governance note**: No project constitution file exists in this checkout. Per the run's stage setup, the repository-root `AGENTS.md` is used as the governance reference in place of `/memory/constitution.md`; this substitution is recorded here, in plan.md, and in research.md R7.
+
+**Assumptions recorded (unattended run)**:
+
+1. The authoring host is x86-64 by four redundant signals (research R6 appendix), so the *expected* outcome is branch (b) — missing observer. Branch (a) applies only if a genuine Windows 11 ARM64 device is at hand when the run executes; T003 fixes the branch at run time.
+2. Zero code changes are planned (plan R8): the change touches at most `docs/install/GETTING_STARTED.md`, `docs/releases/0.1.0.md` (only if a contradiction is found), and one new transcript under `docs/acceptance/`; `Cargo.lock` stays byte-identical.
+3. No workspace-wide build and no full test suite (task directive); the observers are the smallest ones defined in quickstart.md.
+4. The feature spec requests no automated code tests: the plan's Testing note substitutes quickstart scenario observers for unit tests (plan Constitution gate 6 — "No tests are added"). Story "verification" below is therefore scenario-driven capture with inline contract assertions (contracts/version-command.md C1–C5, A1–A5), not red-green TDD steps.
+
+## Format: `[ID] [P?] [Story] Description`
+
+- **[P]**: Can run in parallel (different files, no dependencies)
+- **[Story]**: Which user story this task belongs to (US1, US2, US3 — from spec.md)
+- Every task carries the exact file path(s) it touches
+
+## Path Conventions
+
+Paths are repository-root-relative. This feature touches `docs/**` only, plus creates exactly one new file under `docs/acceptance/`. No source-tree change is planned.
+
+---
+
+## Phase 1: Setup (Shared Infrastructure)
+
+**Purpose**: Establish a trusted baseline before any observation or edit.
+
+- [X] T001 [P] Verify the pinned toolchain and checkout baseline on the authoring host: `cargo +1.97.1 --version` reports 1.97.1 under `rust-toolchain.toml`, `rustup show` records the host triple (expect `x86_64-pc-windows-msvc` on the authoring host per research R6), `git rev-parse HEAD` records the checkout SHA — no file writes; values anchor `docs/acceptance/windows-arm64-<date>.md` (T016) and the PR record
+- [X] T002 [P] Baseline-read the documents this change modifies or verifies, recording their current state for the later diff audit: the platform statement in `docs/install/GETTING_STARTED.md` § 1 (currently "provides verified Windows and Ubuntu x86-64 archives … On macOS or another platform, build from source"), the "Expected last line" block (currently `graphhelm 0.1.0`), and the Downloads table in `docs/releases/0.1.0.md`; read the format references `docs/acceptance/install-rehearsal-2026-09-13.md` and `docs/acceptance/clean-machine-2026-09-14.md` as the transcript templates — no file writes
+
+---
+
+## Phase 2: Foundational (Blocking Prerequisites)
+
+**Purpose**: Fix the branch and capture the one piece of evidence that is branch-independent.
+
+**⚠️ CRITICAL**: T003 fixes branch (a)/(b) (research R6) — US1 task selection and US2/US3 wording all depend on it.
