+## Dependencies & Execution Order
+
+### Phase Dependencies
+
+- **Setup (Phase 1)**: No dependencies — can start immediately (T001 ∥ T002)
+- **Foundational (Phase 2)**: Depends on Setup — T003 fixes the branch; T004 captures the branch-independent negative control; BLOCKS correct US1/US2/US3 wording (informational, not mechanical)
+- **User Stories (Phases 3–5)**: All depend on Foundational completion
+- **Polish (Phase 6)**: Depends on all desired user stories being complete
+
+### User Story Dependencies
+
+- **US1 (P1)**: Can start after Foundational — strictly sequential internally (one device). Under branch (b), T005–T009 collapse to T010.
+- **US2 (P2)**: Can start after Foundational; T011's wording depends on the US1 OUTCOME (T003 branch + T008/T010 results); T011's transcript link presumes the US3 filename convention (`windows-arm64-<YYYY-MM-DD>.md`) — T019 reconciles at landing.
+- **US3 (P3)**: Transcript content consumes US1 captures (T005–T009) or, under branch (b), the T004 negative control. **Phases 4 + 5 land as ONE change** (data-model: "the guide edit and the transcript land in the same change — one review, one merge"); if they are executed separately, complete US3 before pressing merge so T019 can verify the link.
+
+### Within Each User Story
+
+- US1: strictly sequential — T005 → T006 → T007 → T008 → T009 (host identity before install; install before build; build before run; run before binary proof)
+- US2: T011 → T012 → T013 sequential (same file); T014 parallel (different file); T015 last
+- US3: T016 → T017 → T018 sequential (same file); T019 last (touches both guide and transcript)
+
+### Parallel Opportunities
+
+- Phase 1: T001 ∥ T002
+- Phase 2: T003 ∥ T004
+- Phases 4+5: US2 and US3 touch disjoint files except the single link T019 reconciles — after T011 lands, T014 (releases page) ∥ T016–T018 (transcript) can proceed concurrently
+- Phase 6: T020 ∥ T021
+
