+## Implementation Strategy
+
+### MVP First (User Story 1 Only)
+
+1. Complete Phase 1: Setup
+2. Complete Phase 2: Foundational (branch fixed, negative control captured)
+3. Complete Phase 3: User Story 1
+4. **STOP and VALIDATE**: US1 closes as verified-candidate (branch a) or OBSERVER_MISSING (branch b)
+5. Note: US1 alone is not the full requested change (the guide update is the literal request), but it produces every observation the later phases consume — nothing downstream may invent or substitute one
+
+### Incremental Delivery (one landing unit for the documentation)
+
+1. Setup + Foundational → branch fixed, negative control in hand
+2. US1 → run executed on the device (or blocked and recorded)
+3. US2 + US3 together → guide statement + steps + transcript + link land in ONE change (data-model invariant); validate via T015, T019, T022
+4. Polish → delivery record; under branch (b) the report ends `OBSERVER_MISSING: <absent device>`
+
+### Sizing Note
+
+This is a documentation + evidence feature: "parallel team" scaling is limited to the [P] pairs above; no two unmarked tasks share a file, and the on-device run is inherently serial. There is no cross-compile shortcut (research R1/R6): an x86-64 outcome never substitutes for the ARM64 observation.
